This parent cannot receive a safe implementation plan yet. Its decomposition is largely delivered (3a3d53fc, 9c16a3fa, bff22559, c048b081 and f04b6a22 DONE; bfc881dc ARCHIVED by the explicit ban on low-level activation constructors; spike 580ecb5 DONE). The spike's approved 48-site census is the surviving authority: 15 WORLD_ONLY, 26 INGRESS_SUBJECT and 7 NEEDS_PRODUCTION_SEAM, with no honest production writer for WORLD_ONLY state below the admission fence.

The current task-064b9758 bytes and newest-wins ruling make the remaining circularity mechanical, not speculative:
- policy-fact-resolver.ts returns tier:null/truthClass:UNKNOWN;
- bootstrap-policy-services.ts routes it through evaluatePolicy;
- policy-evaluation skips null-tier facts and produces RISK_TIER_UNCLASSIFIABLE/HOLD_UNKNOWN;
- comment-53b3e945 authorizes that fail-closed result and expressly says acceptance is not clearing the refused activations.
The fresh quiet-tree daemon gate on 064b9758 is therefore 21 files / 408 failed tests (comment-5e7530a7), while its focused 3-file/62-test proof and daemon typecheck pass.

This row's rails simultaneously forbid every available escape: no HUMAN_APPROVAL, PolicyRiskTier seed, caller fact, historical ALLOW in generic worlds, low-level activation constructor, or weakening/deleting genuine accepted-ingress coverage. The parent cannot both remove the ALLOW precondition and preserve the only effect.activate acceptance proofs when production is deliberately unable to ALLOW. task-064b9758 is waiting on this row for a green daemon gate, while this row would need 064b9758 (or a new entitled tier authority) to make those accepted worlds reachable.

Required unblock is a newest-wins human/governor ruling choosing one coherent contract: (A) authorize and name a real tier-bearing server authority prerequisite; or (B) amend this parent so the 26 INGRESS_SUBJECT and 7 reservation-binding sites are re-scoped to exact reachable refusal semantics, explicitly acknowledging the retirement/replacement of positive effect.activate coverage. Without that ruling, additional implementation slices would either mint authority or delete safety evidence.
